--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ChannelsPage.tsx is a thin promotion wrapper: it sets a PageContainer (title,
subtitle, copyLink) and embeds <NotificationChannelsView /> verbatim, so the
notification-delivery-channels CRUD (Discord, Slack, Telegram, email, generic
webhook, ntfy, Pushover) lives at /notifications/channels with a real page
title/breadcrumb instead of being a tab inside another page. The page itself
declares no data of its own (the parity manifest records zero dataSources, zero
panels, and exactly two strings — requiredCount=2); the embedded
NotificationChannelsView owns the channel list + delivery-stats feeds
(useNotificationChannels / useNotificationStats) and the four mutations
(useSaveChannel / useDeleteChannel / useToggleChannel / useTestChannel).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 NotificationChannelsView feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.notificationchannelsview.NotificationChannelsView,
P3 prompt 0188) and owns every channel data state for its two cache-then-network
feeds: the stats-tile skeletons vs tiles, the channel loading skeleton, the
hard-error + retry surface, the no-channels empty state, the populated cards with
their freshness chip + stale auto-refresh, the add affordance, the create/edit
modal with the type selector, the per-card test spinner, and the toast queue.
This page is its host: it sets the PageContainer-equivalent header and embeds the
feature view — never re-implementing it (DRY, ADR-006). This mirrors the sibling
admin/TeslaRegionPage (also a 2-string wrapper that embeds the shared
RegionSettings feature view) and notifications/ArchivedPage (embeds InboxBody).

New files (package io.teslasync.android.notifications.channels):
  - ChannelsPageModel.kt   Registration(ROUTE_ID notificationsChannels,
                           WEB_PATH /notifications/channels, SLUG ChannelsPage)
                           + recordChannelsPageOpened (the one PII-safe
                           view.opened diagnostic, P1/S11). No page-level feed —
                           the embedded feature view owns the channel/stats data.
  - ChannelsPage.kt        Stateful entry ChannelsPage(source, logger): records
                           view.opened, builds the feature view's
                           NotificationChannelsViewModel via
                           viewModel(key=SLUG, factory=NotificationChannelsViewModel
                           .factory(source, logger)); stateless ChannelsPageContent
                           (verticalScroll Column: header + NotificationChannelsView)
                           + ChannelsPageHeader (PageTitle + subtitle BodyText +
                           copy-link IconButton writing WEB_PATH to the clipboard).
  - ChannelsPageHost.kt    ChannelsRoute() resolves LocalDataContainer, builds the
                           feature view source over HttpNotificationsRepository
                           (shared resilient client + offline cache) via
                           notificationChannelsViewSource(repository=…);
                           ChannelsPageHost.register() ->
                           PageHosts.register("notificationsChannels"). Idempotent.

Edits (registration + string catalog + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt  import + ChannelsPageHost.register() at process start
                             (after ArchivedPageHost.register()).
  - web/src/i18n/en.json     notifications.channels.{title,subtitle} added to the
                             canonical key set (ADR-014) — the web page previously
                             only had them as inline t() fallback defaults.
  - res/values/strings.xml (+ values-ar, values-he)  2 generated keys
                             translation_notifications_channels_{title,subtitle}
                             inserted in sorted position, generator-identical format
                             (no tokens, no chars needing escaping); ar/he carry the
                             English fallback (placeholder locales, translated=false).
                             copy-link reuses the existing
                             translation_common_copyLink_action.
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:notifications/Channels row (done, 2/2).

Notes:
  - i18n catalog generator: res/values*/strings.xml is AUTO-GENERATED by
    apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts. The committed catalog is ALREADY
    drifted from en.json before this change (gen --check: 11 files / ~10k lines,
    pre-existing, unrelated to this artifact). To avoid sweeping that unrelated
    drift (incl. apple/windows resources) into this page artifact, the two new
    keys were added at the en.json source AND hand-inserted into the three Android
    strings.xml files byte-identically to what emitAndroidStrings()/androidName()/
    renderValue() produce (verified: sorted between nameRequired↔test and
    testing↔toggleFailed; no escapable chars). A future full `gen-i18n.ts` run
    re-emits these exact lines (no conflict). Honest disclosure (no silent drift).
  - SI: no channel field on this surface is unit-bearing — no SI conversion.
  - States: NotificationChannelsView renders loading / empty(no channels) /
    error+retry / content / stale-offline for its bound feeds (verified by the
    shared NotificationChannelsViewModelTest + NotificationChannelsViewUiTest).
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading + copy-link IconButton contentDescription; the feature
    view supplies card/stat/modal/type-chip content descriptions + dynamic/dark
    theme (ADR-015).
  - Layout: the feature view lays out as a non-lazy Column, so it composes safely
    inside the page's outer verticalScroll container.

